    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Here's a summary of the change I made \u2014 \"an invoice amount must be more than zero\" \u2014 implemented full-stack:\n\n**Front-end** (`features/invoices/InvoicesPanel.tsx`): The form already silently rejected non-positive amounts but surfaced nothing. Added an `error` state that, on an invalid submit, renders a `data-testid=\"invoice-form-amount-error\"` alert; it clears when the user edits the amount or submits a valid one. A positive amount still submits normally.\n\n**Server** (`InvoicesPost.java`): Already rejected non-positive amounts (`amount.signum() <= 0`), so no change was needed there \u2014 verified it matches the requirement.\n\n**Database** (`V8__invoice_amount_positive.sql`): New Flyway migration adding a `CHECK (amount > 0)` constraint on the `invoice` table, enforcing the rule at the schema level regardless of insert path.\n\n`npm run typecheck` and `bin/e2e` (both the `@error` and `@core` tests) pass.",
